# Go source is checked out with LF endings on every platform.
#
# gofmt writes LF and `gofmt -l` lists any file whose bytes differ from its
# output, so a CRLF checkout (the default on Windows, where git is installed
# with core.autocrlf=true) failed `.\build.ps1 -Lint` on every Go file while
# the committed content was already clean. Stating the ending here makes the
# checkout agree with the formatter whatever a developer's git config says.
*.go text eol=lf
